n=16 Lonely Runner sedenion-row proof search (codex-2026-05-31 S390)
denominator n=16, moving speeds k=15, threshold=1/16

1. Unit skeleton gate lemma
   Odd points a/16 are the pure sedenion row's unit boundary.
   residue mod16  v2  min_{a odd} ||r*a/16||  verdict
              0 inf                        0  kills units
              1   0                     1/16  safe boundary
              2   1                      1/8  safe boundary
              3   0                     1/16  safe boundary
              4   2                      1/4  safe boundary
              5   0                     1/16  safe boundary
              6   1                      1/8  safe boundary
              7   0                     1/16  safe boundary
              8   3                      1/2  safe boundary
              9   0                     1/16  safe boundary
             10   1                      1/8  safe boundary
             11   0                     1/16  safe boundary
             12   2                      1/4  safe boundary
             13   0                     1/16  safe boundary
             14   1                      1/8  safe boundary
             15   0                     1/16  safe boundary
   Consequence: if no speed is 0 mod 16, every odd a/16 is a lonely
   boundary witness.  So an open-cover counterexample must contain a
   16-gate.  This is a clean proved branch, not just evidence.

2. Half-turn parity attack
   Under t -> t+1/2, even speeds are unchanged and odd speeds flip
   forbidden neighborhoods to the opposite half of the circle.
   residue parity  behavior at threshold 1/16
   even            same forbidden status at t and t+1/2
   odd             cannot forbid both antipodal times
   Proof-shape: pair antipodal times.  Odd speeds can spend budget on
   at most one side of each pair; even speeds descend to the quotient.
   This wants an induction on the dyadic shell vector, not a density
   argument.

